# Skill-bank rules

- Author to `.cursor/skills/meta/skill-authoring-standard/` and validate with
  `python3 tools/lint_skills.py` before finishing.
- Frontmatter `name` must equal the folder name; the bank (parent folder) must be one of:
  general-virality, spotify-mix-content, research-workflows, meta, experimental.
- `metadata` must carry `version` (semver), `maturity`, `confidence`, `evidence_basis`,
  `requires_human_approval`; domain-bank skills also need non-empty `evidence_refs` (claim or
  technique IDs that actually exist).
- New research-generated skills start in `experimental/` with `maturity: experimental`
  (ADR 0005). Any behavioural change bumps `version` and requires a regression record in
  `evaluation/regression/`.
- Keep skills operational: triggers, inputs, steps with completion criteria, testable output
  contract. Background knowledge goes to `knowledge/` and is referenced, not inlined.
- Every technique instruction states its intended viewer behaviour; never promise virality or a
  direct algorithmic effect.
- Do not edit `.agents/skills/` (third-party, lockfile-managed).
